{
  "unitId": "P02",
  "studyPack": {
    "conceptPrimer": [
      {
        "prdId": "P02-PRD01",
        "heading": "Differential Kinematics & Graph Slopes",
        "proseLatex": "$v = \\frac{dx}{dt}$ (slope of the $x$-$t$ graph); $a = \\frac{dv}{dt} = v\\frac{dv}{dx}$ (slope of the $v$-$t$ graph). Signed area under $v$-$t$ gives displacement; unsigned area $\\int|v|\\,dt$ gives total distance. Micro-check: a $v$-$t$ triangle above the axis then an equal one below: displacement $0$, distance $2 \\times \\frac{1}{2}bh$."
      },
      {
        "prdId": "P02-PRD02",
        "heading": "SUVAT & the $n$-th Second Displacement",
        "proseLatex": "Constant $a$: $v = u + at$, $s = ut + \\frac{1}{2}at^2$, $v^2 = u^2 + 2as$, and the $n$-th second displacement $s_n = u + \\frac{a}{2}(2n - 1)$. Micro-check: $u = 0$, $a = 2$: $s_3 = \\frac{2}{2}(5) = 5\\,\\text{m}$ — matches $\\frac{1}{2}(2)(9) - \\frac{1}{2}(2)(4) = 5$."
      },
      {
        "prdId": "P02-PRD03",
        "heading": "Projectile Machinery",
        "proseLatex": "$v_x = u\\cos\\theta$ constant; $a_y = -g$; path $y = x\\tan\\theta - \\frac{gx^2}{2u^2\\cos^2\\theta}$; $R = \\frac{u^2\\sin 2\\theta}{g}$ peaks at $45^\\circ$; $H = \\frac{u^2\\sin^2\\theta}{2g}$. Complementary angles $\\theta$ and $90^\\circ - \\theta$ share range with $H_1/H_2 = \\tan^2\\theta$. Micro-check: $u = 20$, $\\theta = 30°$: $R = \\frac{400\\sin 60°}{10} = 20\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{m}$."
      },
      {
        "prdId": "P02-PRD04",
        "heading": "Apex Physics: $v_y = 0$, Not $v = 0$",
        "proseLatex": "At the top of a projectile, vertical velocity vanishes but horizontal velocity remains: $v_{\\text{top}} = u\\cos\\theta$, and $\\vec{a} = -g\\hat{j}$ is perpendicular to it. Time of flight $T = \\frac{2u\\sin\\theta}{g}$. Micro-check: $\\theta = 60°$, $u = 20$, $g = 10$: $T = 2\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{s}$, $v_{\\text{top}} = 10\\,\\text{m/s}$."
      },
      {
        "prdId": "P02-PRD05",
        "heading": "Relative Velocity",
        "proseLatex": "$\\vec{v}_{AB} = \\vec{v}_A - \\vec{v}_B$: the velocity of $A$ as seen from $B$. Rain-man and boat-river problems reduce to triangle components. Micro-check: boat $5\\,\\text{m/s}$ across a $3\\,\\text{m/s}$ stream: ground speed $\\sqrt{25 + 9} = \\sqrt{34}\\,\\text{m/s}$."
      },
      {
        "prdId": "P02-PRD06",
        "heading": "Circular Kinematics: Inward Acceleration Always",
        "proseLatex": "$v = \\omega r$ (tangential), $a_c = \\frac{v^2}{r} = \\omega^2 r$ pointing radially inward even at constant speed. With speeding up, tangential $a_t = \\alpha r$ combines orthogonally: $a_{\\text{net}} = \\sqrt{a_c^2 + a_t^2}$. Micro-check: $v = 4$, $r = 2$: $a_c = 8\\,\\text{m/s}^2$; if $a_t = 6$, net $= 10\\,\\text{m/s}^2$."
      }
    ],
    "keyFormulas": [
      {
